  "text": "Weight gain, brain zaps, blurred vision\nThis is my second time on Cymbalta.\nI begrudgingly allowed my Rheumatologist prescribe it for Fibro even though I had taken it several years ago and hated it.\nWeaning off this med is brutal.\nThe best way to do it is work with your physician and establish a tapering down schedule.\nWhen you get below 30mg ask your dr. to prescribe lower dosages through a compound pharmacy as they can make it into 20 mg liquid doses x 5cc.\nThe idea is you go down to 20 then 10 then 5 and voilá.\nIt is not painless but it is definitely  more tolerable than just reducing doses to 30mg and skipping days.\nI'm in the process of weaning off it due to weight gain.\n",
